[al:新概念英语第二册]
[ti:Taken for a Ride]
[00:00.96]Why did the writer not get off the bus at Woodford Green? | 为什么作者没有在伍德福德格林下车？
[00:15.17]I love travelling in the country, | 我喜欢在乡下旅行，
[00:18.75]but I don't like losing my way. | 但我不喜欢迷路。
[00:22.04]I went on an excursion recently, | 我最近去了一次短途旅行，
[00:25.35]but my trip took me longer than I expected. | 但我的旅程比我预期的要长。
[00:29.50]'I'm going to Woodford Green,' | “我要去伍德福德格林，”
[00:32.41]I said to the conductor as I got on the bus, | 我上车时对售票员说，
[00:36.48]'but I don't know where it is.' | “但我不知道它在哪里。”
[00:39.96]'I'll tell you where to get off.' answered the conductor. | “我会告诉你哪里下车。”售票员回答。
[00:45.40]I sat in the front of the bus to get a good view of the countryside. | 我坐在巴士前排，以便更好地欣赏乡村景色。
[00:51.62]After some time, the bus stopped. | 过了一会儿，巴士停了下来。
[00:55.44]Looking round, I realized with a shock that I was the only passenger left on the bus. | 我环顾四周，震惊地发现我是车上唯一的乘客了。
[01:03.68]'You'll have to get off here,' | “你必须在这里下车，”
[01:06.71]the conductor said. 'This is as far as we go.' | 售票员说。“我们只能到这里了。”
[01:11.84]'Is this Woodford Green?' I asked. | “这是伍德福德格林吗？”我问道。
[01:15.68]'Oh dear,' said the conductor suddenly. | “哦，天哪，”售票员突然说道。
[01:19.81]'I forgot to put you off.' | “我忘了让你下车了。”
[01:22.80]'It doesn't matter,' I said. 'I'll get off here.' | “没关系，”我说，“我就在这里下车。”
[01:28.04]'We're going back now,' said the conductor. | “我们现在要回去了，”售票员说。
[01:32.29]'Well, in that case, | “好吧，既然如此，”
[01:34.62]I prefer to stay on the bus,' I answered. | 我宁愿留在车上，”我回答道。